WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:05.529
Just like the Haunting of Hill House, Bly
Manor is stuffed with creepy, secret ghosts

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:07.089
watching events from the shadows.

00:00:07.089 --> 00:00:11.719
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'll be revealing all the hidden

00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:15.570
ghosts I found in Bly Manor,
where to find them, and explaining their connection

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.620
to the Lady of the Lake and Flora's dollhouse.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.760
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.390
In the first episode just after Dani arrives,
as Flora shows her around the house and they

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:29.950
go up the stairs, you can spot a figure wearing
a hat lurking in the corner.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:34.550
This is the plague doctor ghost and you can
see him move his head ever-so-slightly upwards

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.710
as if observing Dani's arrival.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:41.109
The plague doctor is introduced in the eighth
episode when he comes to the manor to diagnose

00:00:41.109 --> 00:00:42.530
Viola's sickness.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.570
He's killed around a decade after her death
when he accidentally wanders into the path

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:50.670
of the vengeful Lady of the Lake,
while the manor is being used as a quarantine

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.739
location after a plague outbreak in Bly.

00:00:53.739 --> 00:00:58.539
You can see him next reflected in the mirror
of Dani's room, after Miles wanders in.

00:00:58.539 --> 00:01:02.609
And when Dani is having dinner for the first
time with Mrs Grose and the children,

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:07.590
you can see the plague doctor's beaked mask,
brown coat and gloves just behind Miles and

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.410
in front of the dining room door.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:13.720
He seems to quickly disappear once the camera
moves to a wider shot.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.620
Later after Flora has finished her bath, she
opens the door to her room and you can see

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:20.050
the silhouette of the creepy ghost.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:25.420
Then, after Dani tucks Miles into bed, the
doctor reappears inside the bathroom.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:29.640
And when Dani walks through the bathroom,
you can see his reflection in the mirror.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:34.640
As Dani puts Flora to bed, the plague doctor
can be seen hiding near the window in her

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:35.680
bedroom.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.920
Later that night, you can spot his beak-shaped
mask in this shot here as he silently watches

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.860
Dani coming out of the kitchen;
and then he's here at the end of the corridor.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:51.390
The next day, after Miles shows Dani the spider,
he appears at the end of the garden.

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:56.430
Then as Dani and the kids go back to the house,
he's lurking outside the manor in this shot,

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:59.990
at the same time that Peter Quint's ghost
first appears to Dani.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:05.840
At lunch, the plague doctor appears almost
in plain sight in the kitchen fireplace.

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:10.650
The next time Dani puts Flora to bed, the
plague doctor is watching on yet again, this

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:12.799
time from the corridor.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:18.459
And when Miles comes to ask Dani for a fan,
he's back to lurking in the bathroom.

00:02:18.459 --> 00:02:23.480
This next appearance is very slight, but you
can just spot his hat reflected in the walk-in

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:24.519
closet room mirror here.

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:30.200
He also later watches Dani emerge from Flora's
room after she was locked in the closet by

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.769
the children.

00:02:31.769 --> 00:02:36.439
And then at the very end of the first episode,
the creepy profile of the ghost appears in

00:02:36.439 --> 00:02:37.439
the garden.

00:02:37.439 --> 00:02:42.599
There's a spooky moment in the second episode
when Dani descends into the basement to recover

00:02:42.599 --> 00:02:44.680
Flora's Lady of the Lake doll.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:49.359
As she turns off the light and leaves, hidden
in the pile of discarded old dolls, you can

00:02:49.359 --> 00:02:52.099
spot the Doll Face Ghost sitting up.

00:02:52.099 --> 00:02:56.079
This ghost is the little boy that Flora discovered
playing with her dollhouse.

00:02:56.079 --> 00:02:59.989
He gets his name "Doll Face Ghost" from the
mask that Flora took from another doll in

00:02:59.989 --> 00:03:03.779
the attic and put on him as she said his face
was unfinished.

00:03:03.779 --> 00:03:07.079
The boy became a ghost when he was killed
by the Lady of the Lake during one of her

00:03:07.079 --> 00:03:09.239
walks to her daughter's old room.

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:13.500
You can spot his ghost standing at the end
of a corridor on the ground floor while Dani

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.280
is looking for Miles in the second episode.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.700
In the third episode, you can just make out
his nightgown here outside the door as the

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.819
police officer goes to leave.

00:03:22.819 --> 00:03:26.830
And then moments later, he's back in the house
just behind Dani.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:31.760
The next morning, as Dani's getting up, you
can spot him lurking in the shadows.

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.510
And in a super-creepy moment, he appears in
the mirror of Flora's bedroom where he turns

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:39.269
his head as Dani walks past.

00:03:39.269 --> 00:03:44.200
And you can see him move his head as he watches
Dani leave Flora's room after she kisses her

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.799
goodnight in the fourth episode.

00:03:46.799 --> 00:03:50.590
You can also see him crouched in the corner
of the kitchen here.

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:54.370
Which must be one of his favourite hiding
spots because he's back there in the fifth

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:55.930
episode.

00:03:55.930 --> 00:04:01.189
And during one of Mrs Grose's time loops,
the little boy ghost pops up behind some furniture

00:04:01.189 --> 00:04:03.099
in the main hallway.

00:04:03.099 --> 00:04:07.069
Also hidden in this shot to the right of the
staircase is the ghost of the vicar, sombrely

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:08.069
looking on.

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:12.669
The vicar was the second victim who accidentally
found himself caught in the Lady of the Lake's

00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:14.239
deadly path.

00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:19.169
And he appears again in the fifth episode
in the bathroom between Flora and Miles's

00:04:19.169 --> 00:04:20.169
bedrooms.

00:04:20.169 --> 00:04:24.400
In the third episode, as the police officer
is leaving you can spot a hidden ghost standing

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.710
to attention at the back of the entrance hall.

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.669
We don't know exactly how this soldier died,
but during one of Flora's memories, while

00:04:30.669 --> 00:04:35.620
she was tucked away, her uncle Henry tells
her about a ghost he once knew at Bly Manor.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:38.009
"I had a friend when I was your age, too.

00:04:38.009 --> 00:04:39.720
In this house, in fact.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:43.800
He was a soldier, and I was very afraid of
him, until I gave him a story."

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:47.770
We don't know if Viola's ghost killed this
soldier or if he died of some other cause,

00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:51.930
however, during the Second World War, the
British government requisitioned large country

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.770
houses and estates to serve as part of the
war effort,

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:58.840
and it's quite possible that this soldier
was someone working at Bly Manor at the time

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:02.340
who was unlucky enough to cross paths with
the Lady of the Lake.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:06.509
He also appears behind Miss Jessel as she
plays with Flora's dolls.

00:05:06.509 --> 00:05:11.580
A nice detail in this scene is that the camera
very briefly sharpens its focus on the soldier

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.020
doll just before he shows up behind Rebecca.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:19.699
This next one is tricky to see, but you can
spot the soldier for just a split second when

00:05:19.699 --> 00:05:24.030
the lightning flashes in the kitchen while
Rebecca and Peter are talking together.

00:05:24.030 --> 00:05:28.850
The soldier ghost also appears again towards
the end of a corridor just after the doctor

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:31.319
who's come to check on Flora leaves.

00:05:31.319 --> 00:05:35.430
You'll need to watch this scene carefully
because when the doctor was talking to Dani,

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:40.010
the corridor was empty but after he leaves
the ghost is now there.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:45.620
And in the fourth episode, he's creepily watching
Dani outside while she burns her former fiancé's

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.190
spectacles in the bonfire.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:52.250
Then in the sixth episode, as Dani chases
Flora up the stairs into the attic, you can

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:56.530
spot both the soldier ghost and the vicar
ghost looking on.

00:05:56.530 --> 00:06:00.830
The eighth episode reveals the dark backstory
of Viola and Perdita,

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:06.240
and midway through just before Perdita goes
to ask Arthur to open the trunk, as she descends

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:09.349
the stairs,
the portrait of her dead sister seems to come

00:06:09.349 --> 00:06:16.870
alive and there's a little angry sound in
the air.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:21.680
Some other creepy apparitions that are harder
to identify include these hands grabbing onto

00:06:21.680 --> 00:06:25.169
a chair while Mrs Grose and Owen are eating
in the kitchen,

00:06:25.169 --> 00:06:29.500
meaning there's a ghost hiding under the table,
and judging by the sleeves, it's probably

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:30.909
the Doll Face Ghost.

00:06:30.909 --> 00:06:35.500
There's an unknown ghost at the back of the
entrance hall in the fourth episode wearing

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.780
what looks like breeches and knee-high socks.

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:43.159
And that same figure appears in the doorway
of the chapel when the Wingraves arrive home

00:06:43.159 --> 00:06:45.069
in the fifth episode.

00:06:45.069 --> 00:06:49.410
And there seems to be a ghost lurking at the
back of this corridor which looks like it

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:54.000
might be the Doll Face ghost,
but it's a little too blurry to be sure though

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.780
the hidden figure definitely wasn't there
earlier on the same day.

00:06:57.780 --> 00:07:02.460
There's also a ghostly figure just behind
Jamie, while she and Dani are out looking

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:03.690
for Peter Quint.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:08.580
And its long, light-coloured robe suggests
it could be the Doll Face Ghost again.

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:12.439
And there are even more plague doctor ghost
appearances to look out for on top of the

00:07:12.439 --> 00:07:14.250
ones I mentioned earlier.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:19.530
When Dani bends down to pick up Flora's faceless
doll, as she gets up there's a blurry figure

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:22.600
reflected in the mirror that wasn't there
before.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:26.180
Judging from the brownish colours, it looks
like the plague doctor again.

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:31.599
In the second episode, the masked doctor can
be seen spying on Mrs Grose and Jamie over

00:07:31.599 --> 00:07:32.599
here.

00:07:32.599 --> 00:07:36.699
And as Jamie comes back in the house, he's
right at the end of the corridor.

00:07:36.699 --> 00:07:40.970
During the game of hide-and-seek in the second
episode, you can spot the doctor lurking near

00:07:40.970 --> 00:07:44.690
a window in a room where Dani goes to look
for the children.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:48.780
And during the game, the ghost of Miss Jessel
is watching in the background while Dani's

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.249
back is turned.

00:07:50.249 --> 00:07:54.669
In the third episode, while Dani, Mrs Grose,
Miles and Flora are talking to the police

00:07:54.669 --> 00:07:58.099
officer who's come to investigate Dani's sighting
of Peter Quint,

00:07:58.099 --> 00:08:02.770
in the background you can spot the outline
of the plague doctor's distinctive beaky mask

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:04.729
as he observes the scene.

00:08:04.729 --> 00:08:09.240
And in the fourth episode, you can spot the
creepy hat and beak crouching by the desk

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:12.319
in the study as Dani walks past with a bottle
of wine.

00:08:12.319 --> 00:08:17.150
And there are even a few secret ghosts when
characters aren't at Bly Manor.

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:21.210
It's not immediately obvious, but the backpacker
that comes out of the room Dani's staying

00:08:21.210 --> 00:08:25.210
in at the hostel in London is very likely
another hidden ghost.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:29.479
Notice that Dani's room is for two people,
but only one bed is made up,

00:08:29.479 --> 00:08:33.479
and it's unlikely anyone else has been staying
there as she's been using the sheets from

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:36.630
the second bed to cover up the mirrors in
the room.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:40.610
Another ghost outside the manor you might
have missed is the ghost of Edmund who appears

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:45.589
very briefly in the window of a taxi that
rushes past Dani in the first episode.

00:08:45.589 --> 00:08:50.510
I also have a theory that there could be some
ghosts haunting Miles's boarding school.

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:54.850
These two priests in the headmaster's office
while Miles is being reprimanded seem strangely

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:58.470
silent throughout and not really necessary
for the scene.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:02.320
And when the camera cuts to a different angle,
the priest to the front of the desk seems

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.730
to no longer be there.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:08.010
Likewise, when Miles goes to the school's
chapel to read a passage from the Bible, there's

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:10.290
a mysterious man painting the wall.

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:14.680
He seems like an unnecessary character to
add to this scene given Miles has no interaction

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:19.610
with him, and I suspect he may be a ghost
as well, similar to the clock-fixing ghost

00:09:19.610 --> 00:09:21.250
in Hill House.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:25.440
Like Dani's backpacker ghost, these figures
may simply be there to add to the oppressive

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:29.580
sense Miles already feels from the ghost of
Peter Quint.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:34.100
An interesting detail is that all the hidden
Bly Manor ghosts we need to look out for throughout

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:40.370
the season appear as dolls when Flora introduces
Dani to her dollhouse in the very first episode.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:45.050
Notice that Rebecca Jessel's doll is behind
Flora's bed, which is fitting as the ghost

00:09:45.050 --> 00:09:48.290
of the dead au pair has been taking possession
of Flora.

00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:53.070
Similarly, Peter Quint's doll is hiding behind
the wardrobe in Miles's bedroom.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:57.550
The plague doctor is in the bathroom exactly
where he appears as Dani walks through the

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:58.550
room.

00:09:58.550 --> 00:10:03.260
The Doll Face Ghost is down in the entrance
hall, where he appeared in the fifth episode.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:06.950
As is the soldier ghost who appeared there
in episode three.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:10.990
Perdita is in the attic, which is where she
was killed after opening Viola's trunk of

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:15.860
clothes and jewels, and she's the ghost who
Flora tells to be quiet in the second episode.

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:20.500
I haven't seen the dead vicar in the dining
room [as he is here], but presumably he's

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:23.199
lurking around there in a scene somewhere

00:10:23.199 --> 00:10:26.800
And Mrs Grose is the doll with the red top
and green skirt.

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:31.130
Sneakily, this doll is an early clue to the
fact that Mrs Grose is already dead and is

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:36.440
actually a ghost at this point, something
that isn't revealed until the fifth episode.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:39.700
The other three dolls are for characters that
are still alive:

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.360
Flora, Miles and Dani.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:45.400
As we later find out though, Flora and Miles
have already been possessed by ghosts;

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:49.680
and Dani will eventually become possessed
as well by the Lady of the Lake.

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:53.470
Now if you're as creeped out as me by Bly
Manor's hidden ghosts spying on the home's

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:56.110
inhabitants,
you'll find it troubling to know especially

00:10:56.110 --> 00:11:00.230
